# The busy-peer case, RIGHT half: it does the pressing, and it is the half whose verdict is under
# test. Nothing here is slowed down -- this instance renders in microseconds throughout.
#
# Two presses, and the gap between them is the whole point. The first drives the left half into a
# ten-second render at about eighteen seconds of uptime. The second lands at about twenty-six --
# INSIDE the window where four missed heartbeats have expired the left half's presence here, and
# before that render ends. A press there advances one page instead of two, and the spread is broken
# by nothing worse than the other device being busy.
log pageflip-renderstall-right: start
expect_timeout 90000
expect Entering activity: Home
wait 800
tap confirm
expect Entering activity: EpubReader
expect peer present
# The press that puts the left half into its long render.
wait 15000
tap down
# The press inside the flap.
wait 9000
tap down
wait 8000
screenshot /screenshots/pf-rs-right-00.bmp
wait 4000
log pageflip-renderstall-right: done
quit
